  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Above normal temperatures, at least 5 to 10\ndegrees above average, expected Tuesday through late week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA large high pressure system will move east across the Mid \nAtlantic coast and out to sea on Tuesday. Areas to the N of the \nhigh will be influence by the WSW flow. This will bring mostly \nsunny skies and warm temps well above normal for this time of \nyear. However, the SW flow will keep coastal temps much lower \ndue to the sea breeze. Temperatures likely to be at least 5 to \n10 degrees above normal with the highest temperatures currently \nexpected towards the end of the week. The hot weather should \nalso help to develop some isolated to scattered thunderstorms \neach afternoon beginning Wednesday and continuing through the \nend of the week.",
